# --- trixie-backports: strictly for hardware too new for stable's kernel ---
#
# Debian trixie ships kernel 6.12 LTS, whose amdgpu driver knows GC 11.5.0,
# 11.5.1 and 11.5.2 only. The IRN target laptop (HP OmniBook, AMD Krackan2,
# PCI 1002:1902) reports **GC 11.5.3** -- read straight off the hardware at
# /sys/.../ip_discovery/die/0/GC/0. 6.12 therefore cannot bring the display
# engine up and X falls back to an unaccelerated framebuffer at the wrong
# resolution. Stable's firmware-amd-graphics (20250410) is also missing every
# gc_11_5_3_*.bin blob, so the kernel alone would not be enough.
#
# Backports carries linux-image-amd64 7.1.8 (GC 11.5.0-11.5.4) and
# firmware-amd-graphics 20260622 (ships the 7 gc_11_5_3 blobs). 7.1.8 is the
# exact kernel version verified working against this GPU on 2026-08-30.
#
# This is deliberately NOT a general upgrade channel -- see backports.pref.chroot,
# which makes everything here un-installable except the explicit opt-in list.
deb http://deb.debian.org/debian trixie-backports main contrib non-free non-free-firmware
